5.8 Stratified Proportional Sample

5.8.1 Quota calculation
Site allocations are proportional to each stratum’s share of the total candidate pool. Rounding to whole numbers can cause the quotas to sum to one more or less than TARGET_N; the stratum with the largest rounding remainder absorbs that adjustment.

5.8.1.1 ArcGIS Pro equivalent for quota calculation

Right-click the stratification field column in the attribute table and select Summarize to count the available points per stratum.
In a spreadsheet, divide each stratum count by the total to get proportions, multiply each by TARGET_N, and round to the nearest whole number. Apply a remainder correction if the sum does not equal TARGET_N.


strata_summary &lt;- points_stratified |&gt;
  st_drop_geometry() |&gt;
  count(.data[[STRATIFY_BY]]) |&gt;
  mutate(
    prop      = n / sum(n),
    quota_raw = prop * TARGET_N,
    quota     = round(quota_raw)
  )

# Rounding correction: adjust the stratum with the largest rounding remainder
# so that quotas sum to exactly TARGET_N
discrepancy &lt;- TARGET_N - sum(strata_summary$quota)
if (discrepancy != 0) {
  strata_summary &lt;- strata_summary |&gt;
    mutate(remainder = abs(quota_raw - quota)) |&gt;
    arrange(desc(remainder))
  strata_summary$quota[1] &lt;- strata_summary$quota[1] + discrepancy
}




5.8.2 Sampling
Sites are drawn independently within each stratum using slice_sample().

5.8.2.1 ArcGIS Pro equivalent for sampling
No single ArcGIS Pro tool performs stratified proportional random sampling directly. The closest workflow is:

For each stratum, use Select By Attribute to isolate that stratum’s points.
Use the Subset Features tool (or a Python script with a random sort) to select the quota number of points from that stratum.
Export each stratum’s selection to a temporary layer, then use Merge (Data Management Tools → General) to combine all subsets into one output layer.

The R script handles all strata in a single pipeline.

set.seed(SET_SEED)

field_sites &lt;- points_stratified |&gt;
  group_by(.data[[STRATIFY_BY]]) |&gt;
  nest() |&gt;
  left_join(
    strata_summary |&gt; select(all_of(STRATIFY_BY), quota),
    by = STRATIFY_BY
  ) |&gt;
  mutate(sampled = map2(data, quota, \(d, q) slice_sample(d, n = q))) |&gt;
  unnest(sampled) |&gt;
  ungroup() |&gt;
  st_as_sf()
